    {
        "content": "<p>Howdy,</p>\n<p>Apologies if this is not the right channel for this question. Feel free to redirect me elsewhere if necessary.</p>\n<p>I am learning Lean at the moment and was hoping to get a hint on a problem I am having.</p>\n<p>I am trying to show that the bivariate polynomial (p(x,y)=x^2+y^2) is symmetric. So far, I have been trying to show this using extensionality, as in the code below, but I am unsure how to handle the coefficient function.</p>\n<p>Another approach I considered was checking both permutation maps, since there are only (2!) in this case, and showing equality for each one. However, I am unsure how to set that up. In particular, I am unsure what I would pass to the <code>cases</code> tactic. Would I need to turn <code>Equiv.Perm (Fin 2)</code> into an inductive type somehow? From there, I think the proof would be a straightforward <code>calc</code>.</p>\n<p>Any help or hints would be appreciated. My current infoview and code are below.</p>\n<p>Thanks!</p>\n<p><strong>Infoview:</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Equiv.Perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">coeff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">coeff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><strong>Code:</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> Define p(x,y) = x² + y². -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">basicSymmetric</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> Example: p(x,y) = x² + y² is symmetric. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial.IsSymmetric</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">basicSymmetric</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">basicSymmetric</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial.ext</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 611487486,
        "sender_full_name": "Chuck Garcia",
        "timestamp": 1784431518
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>does <code>fin_cases π</code> do anything?</p>",
